 "summary": "Model of concurrent computation in which actors are the universal primitive: on receiving an asynchronous message an actor can send messages, create actors and choose its behaviour for the next message. Formalised by Clinger and Agha, it underlies Erlang/Elixir processes, Akka, Orleans and Pony.",
